Here's another nasty idea for SporkHack: instead of
a scroll of genocide _eliminating_ a monster
(blesses, monster class), how about if it merely
_decreases_, by some big percent (say, 90%), the
probability of that monster/monster class being
generated _at random_, leaves alone the generation
of monsters/monster classes that are generated in
_fixed quantities per special level_ (so that
special levels stay challenging), and the genocides
stack, so that genociding arch liches twice reduces
their random occurance rate by, say, 99% instead of
90%.

That would make turning the end game trivial quite a
bit harder, if genocide scrolls remain scarce, and
make management of genocides more thought provoking.

